{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/64109-question-about-wolf-blooded-turned-uratha","id":64109,"title":"Question about wolf blooded turned uratha...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-03T10:25:45-08:00","id":64109,"title":"Question about wolf blooded turned uratha...","content":"If a wolf blooded individual had the telekinesis merit and they underwent the first change, would they still have the telekinesis? Or does the first change cost them that ability?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T10:38:47-08:00","id":64119,"title":"","content":"From the GMC: If the character becomes a vampire, ghoul, mage, or any supernatural character type, these Merits disappear. Per the Sanctity of Merits (see p. 158), these Merits can be reallocated.<br /> From Second Sight: When a character gains psychic Merits...he is considered to acquire a lesser template....A character can be subject to only one template at a time, whether greater or lesser. Greater templates such as those at the heart of other World of Darkness games trump lesser templates.<br /> <br /> That said, I've never liked those rules. Though I can imagine people would be upset at the mechanics if people were able to be mage-demon-mummy-vampires. I like the idea that if you're unique before your change (to any supernatural) you can keep and possibly refine that ability. Vampires can pass it along bloodlines, werewolves could have lodges of psychic wolves, mages could do whatever they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T10:42:49-08:00","id":64121,"title":"","content":"I was thinking that. And its only bashing damage. Besides that they'd already lose the wolf blooded merit (arguably becoming something better), but being telekinetic could have limitations for werewolves. Hell would it even work in the Hisil?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T10:48:42-08:00","id":64128,"title":"","content":"I would go ahead and maybe convert it over to some dots in a Gift that seemed appropriate. Or else, if enterprising enough, develop a new Gift based on the psychic numina. Have it be unique to that Uratha. This would keep his &quot;specialness&quot; intact while also not letting everyone get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T10:56:36-08:00","id":64134,"title":"","content":"oh theres a thought! I hadn't thought of that. And they could be a bone shadow so finding such a gift would not be completely out of character","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T15:55:35-08:00","id":64367,"title":"","content":"I would stick with Sanctity of Merits; they lose Telekinesis, but pick up some other merit(s) in its place. For Uratha, cashing out for Fetish or Totem.<br /> <br /> I would not exchange it for a Gift, though. Gifts are granted by spirits, there's no real way to equal that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T17:01:33-08:00","id":64420,"title":"","content":"I'd strip them of the merit as per the books and instead convert it to half Exp they could use for gifts of a similar theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T20:29:48-08:00","id":64544,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a thing. I may well have to do that then. Or just have them stay kin. That could be a fun thing. So how different is combat from the cheat sheet i have in my character sheet pad pdf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T22:20:50-08:00","id":64601,"title":"","content":"Combat is pretty much the same, Defense tends to be a little higher and attack pools smaller. Weapons don't add dice but do automatic damage, generally the pre-GMC rating minus 1 as a rule of thumb. So if I swing a machete (2L) at my target, if I hit, I do successes +2 automatic damage. Dodging means you take a number of dice equal to the double of your defense and roll them, each success negating one of your opponents. That's about the basics of it, can download the GMC rules update for free for more info.<br /> <br /> GMC Rules Update: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-The-God-Machine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...e-Rules-Update</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T22:44:16-08:00","id":64617,"title":"","content":"Yeah i've downloaded that. Im just mind numbed at figuring out apocalypse combat rules previously, and it looks like forsaken has a different style. Is there even an accuracy roll? Or is it strait damage roll after all the subtractions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T23:02:39-08:00","id":64622,"title":"","content":"Accuracy roll? Sorry, been a while since I played Classic WoD. You gain modifiers to your pools, depending on circumstances, yes. Such as if you attack a prone enemy in melee, it's worth a +2 bonus. Likewise, you can decide you specifically want to hit your opponent in the head and take a -3 penalty on the roll, success meaning you do so. You can aim with a firearm for +1 per turn of aiming, cap of +3. Your successes on the attack roll are your damage;<br /> <br /> Bob the Werewolf gets really angry at Jim the uppity human. Bob shifts into his near human form and picks up a baseball bat (1L) to clobber Jim. Bob has Strength 4 and Weaponry 3 with a specialty in baseball bat, so his base attack pool is 8 dice. Jim is a quick little bastard, possessing Dexterity and Wits 3 and Athletics 2 which gives him a Defense of 5. It's clear weather, no marbles on the ground or anything, so combat pools are just straight up without modifiers. Bob acts first and goes after Jim, swinging his bat, and Jim's Defense of 5 is subtracted from Bob's pool of 8 for 3 dice total. Bob rolls well and gets 2 successes, adding to his baseball bat's damage rating of 1, and cracks Jim for 3 damage. Jim was wearing a leather jacket, however, which has grants Armor 1/0. Jim subtracts 1 from Bob's damage, taking 2 Lethal wounds.<br /> <br /> And so on and so forth. Potential modifiers are listed under the different skills <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Sorry, I hope this helps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T23:07:21-08:00","id":64625,"title":"","content":"The GMC era rules are basically an accuracy roll with damage and armor being automatic based on the results of the attack roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T11:50:39-08:00","id":65032,"title":"","content":"whoa whoa whoa, a dice roll is considered a success if its 8 or above?! That seems a touch steep to me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T11:55:10-08:00","id":65037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/64109-question-about-wolf-blooded-turned-uratha?p=65032#post65032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">whoa whoa whoa, a dice roll is considered a success if its 8 or above?! That seems a touch steep to me!</div> </div> </div> </div>The vast majority of instant actions in nWoD only require one success. This did not change with the GMC Rules Update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T12:06:26-08:00","id":65043,"title":"","content":"This is true but in combat? Or is this just a testament to how broken garou were in apocalypse? I remember reading about Frenzy and the instant healing and thinking &quot;damn these guys are nigh unkillable&quot; unlike Uratha and Death Rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T15:26:52-08:00","id":65188,"title":"","content":"Well combat is one of the usual exceptions in wich you need to get as much successes as you can as each is a Health level of damage you'll cause. Auto-damage from weapons helps a bit with that (specially since Defense got a considerable boost, further reducing the usual comabt dice pools).<br /> <br /> Both Requiem and Forsaken were so afraid of being similar to Masquerade and Apocalypse that they went the whole oposite direction, nerfing things like it were going out of style. Some werewolf abilities suffered a lot from that, particularly the &quot;War form&quot; wich boosts aren't that great compared to other forms and has two big penalties in the form of a short duration and the threat of Death Rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T16:41:17-08:00","id":65223,"title":"","content":"Well, technically, in combat you only need a single success to have a noticeable effect, it's just that it's a resisted action, so the effect scales based on how many successes you've achieved. So it isn't really an exception anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T17:33:51-08:00","id":65259,"title":"","content":"No reason I can't adjust the difficulty of success though right? I don't understand why an Uratha with 4 str and melee-5 would still have a difficulty of 8 to hit something. Should be a hell of a lot easier for a skilled individual to crack skulls with a stick yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T17:44:47-08:00","id":65269,"title":"","content":"Because the concept of 'Difficulty' is an OWoD ism. The target number is not a degree of difficult, that comes in at dice rolled, and penalties you might have. A success is a success is a success. You only need one to succeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T17:54:51-08:00","id":65272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/64109-question-about-wolf-blooded-turned-uratha?p=65259#post65259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No reason I can't adjust the difficulty of success though right? I don't understand why an Uratha with 4 str and melee-5 would still have a difficulty of 8 to hit something. Should be a hell of a lot easier for a skilled individual to crack skulls with a stick yes?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>that is what all those dice are for</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T20:39:32-08:00","id":65359,"title":"","content":"With 4 Strength and 5 Brawl you'd have 9 dice to roll.<br /> If any of those get an 8, you hit.<br /> For every one that gets an 8, 9 or 10, you do a point of damage. If you get a 10, you can reroll and theoretically get more than your dicepool worth of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T21:03:51-08:00","id":65372,"title":"","content":"Well i'll say this about the new world combat. It seems a hell of a lot simpler than that of classic world of darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T03:13:37-08:00","id":65522,"title":"","content":"It's definitely more streamlined. On the plus side, in NWoD you need an 8 or higher to succeed but 1's don't cancel successes except in rare and noted situations. So if you've got five dice and roll 1, 1, 8, 9, 9 then you got 3 successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}